### 2. Value Function Approximation (VFA)

#### Files Created
- [backend/vfa/nn_vfa.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/vfa/nn_vfa.py) - Neural Network VFA
- [backend/vfa/dl_vfa.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/vfa/dl_vfa.py) - Deep Learning VFA
- [backend/vfa/feature_engineering.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/vfa/feature_engineering.py)

#### Architecture

**NN-VFA (3-layer MLP)**
```
Input (20) → Dense(128) → ReLU → Dense(64) → ReLU → Dense(32) → ReLU → Output(1)
```

**DL-VFA (4-layer with regularization)**
```
Input (20) → Dense(256) → BatchNorm → ReLU → Dropout(0.2)
          → Dense(128) → BatchNorm → ReLU → Dropout(0.2)
          → Dense(64) → BatchNorm → ReLU
          → Dense(32) → BatchNorm → ReLU → Output(1)
```

#### Features
✅ 20-dimensional state representation:
- Inventory levels (5 features)
- Demand (4 features)
- Time information (3 features)
- Risk scores (2 features)
- Resource availability (2 features)
- Geographic features (2 features)
- Urgency (2 features)

✅ Pre-training with synthetic data
✅ Save/load functionality
✅ Training utilities with experience replay

---

### 3. Approximate Dynamic Programming (ADP)

#### Files Created
- [backend/adp/state_representation.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/adp/state_representation.py)
- [backend/adp/action_space.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/adp/action_space.py)
- [backend/adp/reward_function.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/adp/reward_function.py)
- [backend/adp/transition_model.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/adp/transition_model.py)
- [backend/adp/adp_solver.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/adp/adp_solver.py)

#### Features
✅ **State Space**: Inventory, demand, time, vehicles, risk scores
✅ **Action Space**: Allocate X units from warehouse Y to zone Z
✅ **Reward Function**:
- Deprivation penalty: -1000 per unit unmet demand
- Transportation cost: -50 INR per km
- Priority bonus for urgent deliveries
- Time penalty for delayed response

✅ **Transition Model**: Simulates inventory updates, demand reduction, vehicle management
✅ **Policies**: Greedy and epsilon-greedy for exploration
✅ **Value Iteration**: Uses VFA for value estimation

---

### 4. Optimization Engine (OR-Tools)

#### Files Created
- [backend/optimization/vehicle_routing.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/optimization/vehicle_routing.py)
- [backend/optimization/uav_allocation.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/optimization/uav_allocation.py)
- [backend/optimization/optimizer_engine.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/backend/optimization/optimizer_engine.py)

#### Features
✅ **Vehicle Routing Problem (VRP)**:
- OR-Tools RoutingIndexManager and RoutingModel
- Capacity constraints (5000 kg per truck)
- Distance matrix using haversine formula
- Multi-vehicle route optimization
- Guided local search metaheuristic

✅ **UAV Allocation**:
- Priority scoring (accessibility + medical + urgency)
- Range constraints (100 km for UAVs)
- Capacity constraints (50 kg per UAV)
- Remote area prioritization

✅ **Human-in-the-Loop**:
- Constraint management (avoid routes, disable UAVs, prioritize medical)
- Recalculation with new constraints
- Constraint validation

---

### 5. Forecasting Models

#### Files Created
- [ml-fastapi/forecasting_service/models/arima_forecaster.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/ml-fastapi/forecasting_service/models/arima_forecaster.py)
- [ml-fastapi/forecasting_service/models/garch_forecaster.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/ml-fastapi/forecasting_service/models/garch_forecaster.py)
- [ml-fastapi/forecasting_service/models/ensemble.py](file:///C:/Users/Srish/Desktop/ReliefNet/ml-fastapi/forecasting_service/models/ensemble.py)

#### Features
✅ **ARIMA**: Statsmodels SARIMAX with seasonal components (P, D, Q, s) = (1, 1, 1, 7)
✅ **GARCH**: Volatility modeling for surge prediction using arch library
✅ **Ensemble**: Weighted combination (ARIMA: 30%, GARCH: 20%, Simple: 50%)
✅ Confidence intervals and surge probabilities
✅ 7-day forecast horizon

